### Phase 3: Implement BNF Semantic Actions

Create rule subclasses that build Grammar objects:

- [ ] **`Chalk::Grammar::BNF::Rule::Grammar`**
  ```perl
  package Chalk::Grammar::BNF::Rule::Grammar;
  use experimental 'class';

  class Chalk::Grammar::BNF::Rule::Grammar :isa(Chalk::GrammarRule) {
      method evaluate($context) {
          my %patterns;
          my @rules;

          # Extract from LineList child
          my $line_list = $context->child(0);

          # Process each line (recursively unwrap LineList)
          while (defined $line_list && ref($line_list) eq 'ARRAY') {
              my ($line, $rest) = @$line_list;

              if (ref($line) eq 'HASH' && $line->{type} eq 'pattern') {
                  $patterns{$line->{name}} = $line->{regex};
              }
              elsif (ref($line) eq 'ARRAY') {
                  push @rules, $line;  # Grammar rule
              }
              # Ignore undef (comments/blank lines)

              $line_list = $rest;
          }

          # Build and return Grammar object
          return Chalk::Grammar->build_grammar(rules => \@rules);
      }
  }
  ```

- [ ] **`Chalk::Grammar::BNF::Rule::PatternDef`**
  ```perl
  class Chalk::Grammar::BNF::Rule::PatternDef :isa(Chalk::GrammarRule) {
      method evaluate($context) {
          # % IDENT % = / REGEX / FLAGS
          my $name = $context->child(1);        # IDENT
          my $regex = $context->child(7);       # REGEX content
          my $flags = $context->child(9) // ''; # Optional FLAGS

          # Compile regex with flags
          my $compiled = qr/(?$flags:$regex)/;

          return {
              type => 'pattern',
              name => $name,
              regex => $compiled
          };
      }
  }
